      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Embracing and poking fun at stereotypes can lead to rich comedic opportunities. For a South Asian character, common archetypes include the \"nerdy difference maker\" (e.g., being the tech expert in the family), the \"overly critical\" parent (practicing excessive expectations), or the accent/pronunciation contrast (comparing Indian English to Western stereotypes). You could also explore other tropes like the \"��operations\" stand-in ( fier Overwatch-competitive sibling), or struggling with Angular pointers in Crash Indian classmate, class laundry prop cry regimes.",
